===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# an actual, [[real]] one; notably:
## {{lb|en|finance}} something actually received; real receipts, as distinct from estimated ones.
## {{lb|en|military}} a radio [[callsign]] [[modifier]] that specifies the commanding officer of the unit or asset denoted by the remainder of the callsign and not the officer's assistant or other designee.
##: {{ux|en|Bravo Six '''Actual''', this is Charlie One. Come in, over.|footer=The radio operator is requesting to speak to the commander of the unit under the call sign "Bravo Six", as opposed to any available member of the unit.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[reality|Reality]], usually with the definite article.
#* {{RQ:Landon Ethel Churchill|page=161|volume=I|passage=There was that desolate air about the chamber which is peculiar to an ill-furnished London room: cities need luxuries, were it only to conceal the '''actual'''.}}

